Antivirus definition-signing public key — build-time staging.

Before building an ISO, place the Aether AV Ed25519 public key PEM here as:

    aether-av.pub.pem

live-build copies everything in this includes.chroot tree into the image, so
the file lands at /usr/share/aether/updates/aether-av.pub.pem — the exact path
DEFAULT_PUBLIC_KEY in aether-av.py reads. AETHER_AV_PUBLIC_KEY can override it
for tests and local runs.

Only the PUBLIC key belongs in this repository or any ISO. Generate the AV
keypair offline and keep the private key outside the repo. Definition sets are
signed with scripts/signing/sign_release over the canonical JSON form; the
matching detached 64-byte Ed25519 signature is published as <defs>.sig next to
aether-av-sigs.json in the release assets.

Fail-closed behavior: if the public key, definition file or signature is
absent, --check reports SIGNATURE_MISSING and no file is quarantined. If any of
them is present but malformed, tampered, wrong-schema or expired, --check
reports SIGNATURE_INVALID, and --update writes nothing and acts on no hash.
The AV never fetches and applies unsigned JSON.
